{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing","id":629743,"title":"Humans and Changelings (Balancing)?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-17T02:42:16-07:00","id":629743,"title":"Humans and Changelings (Balancing)?","content":"So I am working on a campaign that kind of goes long the lines of Grimm (the television show) where some characters can be changelings while other players can choose to play as a human who so happens to be friendly to the changelings. The question I have is: are the starting mortals and changelings already balanced, or will I have to give the mortals something special to put them on par with the changeling characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:20:51-07:00","id":629837,"title":"","content":"You'll have to give the humans alot to compensate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T10:03:14-07:00","id":629997,"title":"","content":"Question: Do they need to be on par?<br /> <br /> One of the cool things about stories like this is finding out how the normal humans keep up. They often become the more interesting characters because their circumstances breed the greatest amount of conflict, and the way they deal with that tend to be very clever or bad ass because they push more to keep up.<br /> <br /> Balance is a matter of who can do the most with what they got, not some arbitrary balance of numbers. I'd actually say let your players have a run without extras and see what they do to scrape their wins. If it's too much, you can always retroactively hand them 5 or 10 EXP to give them a boost. But I think you'd be surprised how well they can keep up on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T11:58:21-07:00","id":630129,"title":"","content":"Okay. I was thinking of just giving the human(s) a skill advantages in the occult because of it being their friend(s) being abducted by the true Fae. Perhaps even giving them an &quot;heirloom&quot; like weapon that they could use that would have a secret ability when they use it.<br /> <br /> I guess I don't need them to be too on par I just want to encourage players to use them in this campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T00:48:27-07:00","id":630788,"title":"","content":"One way to go, is to have humans focus on the supernatural merits which they even could have gotten from oaths with various changelings. Doing so also has the added benefit of integrating the mortals into Changeling society and to have them enscorcelled from the start. Alternatively you could look at the endowments of Hunter.<br /> <br /> As for balance, in a perfect world where the Storyteller manages it perfectly, game mechanical power differences can be compensated for through the story. I have rarely played in such a perfect place though. The Storyteller has to be very aware of each characters' strength and weaknesses and make sure they each get equal attention. It is easy for the player of a weak character to feel useless, and such is never good for the game. Furthermore, you also need to make sure your players are up to it and that they also grasp the consequences of their choices. Story attention is not enough for everybody <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T02:47:34-07:00","id":630889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One way to go, is to have humans focus on the supernatural merits which they even could have gotten from oaths with various changelings. </div> </div> </div>Alright, I will have to look into that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively you could look at the endowments of Hunter. </div> </div> </div>My only problem with that is that I don't have the Hunter: the Vigil book. Currently the only new World of Darkness books I have is the core rule book, Changeling: the Lost and Vampires: the Requiem (which I just can't see myself being able to work vampires into a story based largely around changelings).<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> One thought that did come to mind was that perhaps the human player could somehow have had some influence in the changelings escape. Not sure how that would work seeing that mortals can't go to Arcadia unless they are taken there by the true Fae but who knows.<br /> <br /> Is it possible I could create a relic that only the human players could use that could somehow benefit the changeling players? That way it would be in the best interest of the changelings to aid and protect their human allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T03:22:06-07:00","id":630902,"title":"","content":"Actually there is going to be a minor template for Humans who have gone into the hedge on their own looking for the person close to them who was taken. Some even make it all the way to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Edit: At least come 2ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T03:29:11-07:00","id":630914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually there is going to be a minor template for Humans who have gone into the hedge on their own looking for the person close to them who was taken. Some even make it all the way to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Edit: At least come 2ed. </div> </div> </div>Wait does that mean my Changeling: the Lost book that I just bought last week is going to be useless? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T06:44:03-07:00","id":631110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing?p=630914#post630914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait does that mean my Changeling: the Lost book that I just bought last week is going to be useless? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. New editions do not suddenly make it impossible for you to run the game in the old edition. The 2nd edition rule updates for nWoD can be downloaded for free from drivethru rpg (godmachine update from memory) and I have been using them in my 1e game without a problem. Our group likes them. As for the rest, I am not sure I will buy and use them in my current campaign, but nobody is forcing us to do so <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It should be noted that in 1e Changeling it is mentioned that mortals also travel to Arcadia and have managed to rescue their loved ones. It is pretty common theme in fairy tales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:58:33-07:00","id":631245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing?p=631110#post631110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the rest, I am not sure I will buy and use them in my current campaign, but nobody is forcing us to do so <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not! Onyx Path's team of edition ninjas is still in training. They won't be able to compel compliance at swordpoint until at least November. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, seriously, do not worry about it. As with every edition change in every game, there will be some wholesale switching to the new version, some sticking with the old, and a lot of tables combining elements they like from both. Of the 2e changes I've heard, I think I regard all/most of them as making a stronger game. Even so, for various reasons, I may prefer to actually play with a couple of things closer to their 1e forms.* It's a personal thing for each individual to feel out.<br /> <br /> * Or, if I'm honest, their 1e forms as heavily filtered/refined by the passage of time, incomplete memory, and unobserved thought. ^_^<br /> <br /> If it helps, many people have said they felt 1e was pretty much perfect. You certainly won't have a bad game on your hands by any stretch; it's built up a healthy following for a reason. It also has the unquestionable advantage that all of its supplements are already out, whereas there'll be a bit of a wait on 2e. When and if you decide to pick up 2e, you can make decisions about how many and which elements to use from each edition.<br /> <br /> If you're curious about any changes, you can find the open development blog posts up <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/worldofdarkness/changelingthelost/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and the 2e outline is available <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">here</a>. Plenty of people will be happy to answer any questions you have about other tidbits that may have been dropped on the forums. Same story if you'd prefer to keep on point with questions about the edition that's actually out.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Enough of that tangent. Madfox11 is also right that mortals can travel to Arcadia; they sometimes chance on openings to the Hedge. Not everyone who goes there comes back a Changeling. An alternative includes the mortal PCs being brought in by a motley, going on a rescue mission for one or more mutual recently taken (Changeling PC) friends.* Or the mortals may have also been taken, but weren't in Arcadia long enough to become one of the Lost. You've got options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T09:57:12-07:00","id":631275,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the mechanics aren't too hard to port over from any 1E books over to 2E books, and visa versa. There's no reason you have to buy 2nd Edition though.<br /> <br /> Buuuut speaking as a playtester, you'll want a copy when it comes out, There's a lot of good stuff in here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T10:45:54-07:00","id":631306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing?p=631275#post631275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buuuut speaking as a playtester, you'll want a copy when it comes out, There's a lot of good stuff in here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I didn't know you were a playtester, Arc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cool. Here's hoping it's going well, and I'm glad your critical eyes are tuned on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:10:44-07:00","id":631319,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Sooner or later I intend to get some Actual Plays up here in regards to stuff we're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T12:07:15-07:00","id":631387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 2nd edition rule updates for nWoD can be downloaded for free from drivethru rpg (godmachine update from memory) and I have been using them in my 1e game without a problem. </div> </div> </div>Alright that is good to know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> So any feedback on this idea?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it possible I could create a relic that only the human players could use that could somehow benefit the changeling players? That way it would be in the best interest of the changelings to aid and protect their human allies. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T12:49:39-07:00","id":631419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing?p=630889#post630889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible I could create a relic that only the human players could use that could somehow benefit the changeling players? That way it would be in the best interest of the changelings to aid and protect their human allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is certainly a valid option, though I don't know of anything offhand. I'm afraid I don't know what to add; maybe a magical iron object that's quite effective in some way against fey adversaries/magic, but burns any who touch it. Changelings couldn't use it themselves, but would welcome the assistance against fey stuff coming their way.<br /> <br /> If the end is &quot;incentivize Changeling and human PCs to play nice and benefit from doing so,&quot; I really would second the insane vulpine's suggestion of using oaths. It may not be immediately apparent, but they can give both sides of the arrangement some real advantages. Ensorcellment alone -- without which the mortals can't really perceive most fey stuff outside of the Hedge or Arcadia -- is all but a given: the mortals will want it for obvious reasons, and Changelings will find it very useful to have mortal allies who can see all of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing?p=630788#post630788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way to go, is to have humans focus on the supernatural merits which they even could have gotten from oaths with various changelings. Doing so also has the added benefit of integrating the mortals into Changeling society and to have them enscorcelled from the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 08-18-2015, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T18:13:46-07:00","id":631799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the end is &quot;incentivize Changeling and human PCs to play nice and benefit from doing so,&quot; I really would second the insane vulpine's suggestion of using oaths. </div> </div> </div>Alright, are there any good oaths in the book I should use or should I custom make one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T19:44:09-07:00","id":631836,"title":"","content":"Custom make. And encourage your players to come up with the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T20:20:49-07:00","id":631844,"title":"","content":"Okay, so far the plan is to use an oath (will come up with something once the players get around to making their characters).<br /> <br /> Now would it be alright if I had a weapon created for the human players that could provide them an advantage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T22:37:11-07:00","id":631915,"title":"","content":"Sure, it would be especially appropriate if it were a storied weapon from Armory Reloaded.<br /> <br /> You mentioned you wer