Hunter: the Vigil book. So I will try to make that work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also going to be the 2nd edition Fae-Touched, of which have been discussed in the open development already. May be worth checking out the Changeling:the Lost articles on the Onyx Path home page. </div> </div> </div>I actually didn't hear anything about that until this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T04:09:08-07:00","id":633324,"title":"","content":"Could always work with Second sight mortals and work your way through that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T12:40:45-07:00","id":633715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightout</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing?p=633324#post633324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could always work with Second sight mortals and work your way through that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second Sight mortals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T19:53:38-07:00","id":634182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing?p=633715#post633715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second Sight mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>World of Darkness: Second Sight</i> is a book covering how to use mortal characters who for whatever reason have access to psychic powers or traditional thaumaturgy. It contains a lot of the 1e predecessors to the Supernatural Merits found in 2e's rules update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T20:07:45-07:00","id":634212,"title":"","content":"I was in a game where the GM said we could be Changelings, Vampires, or mortals. They all got the same XP, but mortals got the incentive of one free &quot;back from the dead&quot; card; when they were in a situation where they'd die, they got a miraculous escape, one time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T00:13:35-07:00","id":634331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing?p=632020#post632020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kind of like that actually. Now I just need to figure out how storied weapons work.</div> </div> </div> </div> They aren't that complicated, so if you don't want to buy Armory reloaded just for them, storied weapons are magic items that aren't important because they're magical, but are magical because they're important. <br /> <br /> Generally they become magical after gaining historic importance, but some people apparently know techniques to give a destiny to an item as they make it. <br /> <br /> An example is a pistol that generates its own bullets and can be used to kill the dead as well as the living, but the bullets are formed from the user's life force, or dracula's nigh indestructible sword that drinks down blood and souls but using it is automatically a sin. <br /> <br /> The Brother Grimm's book might help the human identify fae things and allow the owner to storycraft but at the cost of emotional detachment or narcissism, the huntsman's ax might slide through magical protections like butter and do agg damage but make the owner obligated to save people, stuff like that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T15:18:33-07:00","id":635093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was in a game where the GM said we could be Changelings, Vampires, or mortals. They all got the same XP, but mortals got the incentive of one free &quot;back from the dead&quot; card; when they were in a situation where they'd die, they got a miraculous escape, one time. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... sounds pretty interesting I might try to use that. Out of curiosity how well do Vampires work with Changelings and mortals?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Brother Grimm's book might help the human identify fae things and allow the owner to storycraft but at the cost of emotional detachment or narcissism, the huntsman's ax might slide through magical protections like butter and do agg damage but make the owner obligated to save people, stuff like that. </div> </div> </div>Sounds pretty cool. Might try that.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the Huntman's axe I was thinking of making it a potential reward for the human players (changelings don't gain any of the benefits of it when using it) that would have a few hidden abilities that the player could unlock as they learned more about its past. At first they would only know of it as a &quot;strange axe&quot; and slowly as they learned its history they would find out that it is the huntsman's axe.<br /> <br /> Is that a good idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T15:49:34-07:00","id":635114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing?p=635093#post635093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm... sounds pretty interesting I might try to use that. Out of curiosity how well do Vampires work with Changelings and mortals?<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>No one ended up playing them, actually. The anticipated balance was that vamps would be slightly better when it came to combat, survival, and magic, but had worse weaknesses and were shut out of a portion of the plot (because they'd be asleep).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T00:52:58-07:00","id":639945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/629743-humans-and-changelings-balancing?p=635093#post635093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds pretty cool. Might try that.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the Huntman's axe I was thinking of making it a potential reward for the human players (changelings don't gain any of the benefits of it when using it) that would have a few hidden abilities that the player could unlock as they learned more about its past. At first they would only know of it as a &quot;strange axe&quot; and slowly as they learned its history they would find out that it is the huntsman's axe.<br /> <br /> Is that a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, storied weapons don't generally work like that, but just make it part of the story. Storied weapons don't generally care who uses them, but if the fae are anethama too it, it makes sense. <br /> <br /> As for it's powers being shy, well I could see playing with the story for that one too. <br /> <br /> Some folklorists think the story has its origin in norse mythology. <br /> <br /> Norse magic was all about knowledge, like odin's sacrifice of his eye for wisdom.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the huntsman was one of Odin's poet warriors, or the ax handle has runes carved in it, that one must understand before unlocking it's full power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}